WEBVTT

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.200
Excuse me, guys and gals...

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:12.360
I'm Satou Hikaru from Class 4.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.450
Th-That's him! That's the guy! 
The transfer student!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.950
Is the son of Shigeno Goro, 
the pro baseball player, in your class?

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.760
That would be him right here.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.300
This is Shigeno Jr. AKA Daigo!

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.210
Riko...

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.090
Oh? You're Daigo-kun?

00:00:33.560 --> 00:00:34.760
Nice to meet y—

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.180
Sorry, but I don't take requests 
for autographs and stuff.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.600
Dad's not around, anyway. 
He's in Taiwan.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:45.530
Huh?

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.700
Oh, man, you sure jumped to conclusions.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:54.780
I didn't want your dad's autograph.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:57.990
My papa's more famous, anyway.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.490
What?!

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:00.830
"Papa"?

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:04.920
My papa has led the majors
 in homeruns before,

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.750
and he retired last year.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.920
I'm sure you've heard of him. Satou Toshiya.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:18.730
<i>Th-The son of Satou Toshiya, 
the man Pop won the World Series with?</i>

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:57.320
If I Wasn't the Second

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:56.070
You're Satou Toshiya's son?

00:02:57.640 --> 00:02:59.150
You mean, <i>the</i> Satou Toshiya?

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:03.570
To be honest, I would've liked 
to have stayed in New York.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:07.220
But since my family's moved back to Japan,

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:09.540
transferring to this school 
was my only real option.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.210
Understand?

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.250
<i>What the hell's with this guy?</i>

00:03:13.630 --> 00:03:15.960
<i>He's annoying the crap 
out of me on every level.</i>

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:19.670
Anyway, I was looking to join 
a local baseball team.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.740
I figured you'd know the score on
that front. Know a good team I can join?

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.180
I mean, you're <i>obviously</i> 
on a team yourself, right?

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.810
Back off! I'm not on any team!

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:30.810
I... see.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.460
Huh? I thought Shigeno-kun played baseball.

00:03:34.460 --> 00:03:35.800
Didn't you know?

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.360
He quit playing a long time ago.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:43.110
Ah! Why don't you refer him to
the team you used to play for?

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.920
You have the coach's 
contact information, right?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:49.100
The Dolphins are a rubber-ball team nowadays.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:54.120
You want to play hardball, right?

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:57.090
Go do some research and 
figure it out for yourself.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.300
Why should I care?

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.470
He's a bit of a grump, isn't he?

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.720
Is he always like that?

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:06.300
Huh?

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:08.920
Well...

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.920
<i>So he's a "second," too, huh?</i>

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.700
<i>His eyes were glinting with confidence.</i>

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:24.920
<i>I bet he's really good at baseball.</i>

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.740
Shigeno-kun!

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.690
Sakura?

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.210
Can we walk home together?

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:37.210
Huh? Where'd that come from?

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.940
Not that I mind.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:48.540
You know, we went to the same 
kindergarten and the same grade school,

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:50.980
but we've never really talked, have we?

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:55.480
Well, we haven't been in
the same class till this year.

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:56.920
So how did you see me?

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:57.560
Huh?

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:01.030
In all that time, 
how did you see me?

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.240
Wh-What do you mean?
Nothing special, really.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.530
A-Anyway, where did all this come from?

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:11.120
Makes sense.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:14.280
There's no reason someone like you 
would give me a second thought.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:15.210
Huh?

00:05:16.030 --> 00:05:18.100
But it's not the same for me.

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:22.350
You've been a celebrity from day one.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.300
You're the son of a pro baseball player,

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.440
which always made you
popular with the other kids.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:30.610
And you always got lots of chocolates 
from girls on Valentines' Day.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:35.240
For a nobody like me, you were always 
someone who was unapproachable.

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:37.930
Oh, come off it.

00:05:37.930 --> 00:05:40.330
All of that is because of my dad.

00:05:40.330 --> 00:05:42.730
I'm not popular because of who I am.

00:05:42.730 --> 00:05:44.570
It's because of who he is.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:46.220
That's not true!

00:05:47.170 --> 00:05:49.040
That's not even the slightest bit true.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:52.360
At least, it wasn't up until 
the moment you quit baseball.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:57.960
You know, my older brother played 
for the Dolphins till last year.

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:01.460
So I used to go watch the games 
with my parents all the time.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:06.420
I saw you play in a bunch of 
games and practice sessions.

00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:10.930
To me, your being a "second" and your 
father being famous didn't come into it.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.470
All I saw was you, giving it your all.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:16.950
You looked so cool out there.

00:06:20.320 --> 00:06:26.900
That's why I've been wanting to ask you
why you quit baseball for a long time now.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:31.950
I'd really love to see you 
play baseball again.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.620
Why does everyone have to
be so annoying about it?

00:06:35.690 --> 00:06:37.160
Just shut up!

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:38.870
And leave me alone, idiot!

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:43.200
He didn't...

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.620
Who <i>does</i> that?

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:47.260
Is this what he's really like?!

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.080
I can't believe it!

00:06:49.080 --> 00:06:52.330
Give me back my first love, you doofus!

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.560
<i>Saying I looked "cool"...</i>

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.810
<i>What the hell was that idiot on about?</i>

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:05.820
<i>I quit because I looked like a loser.</i>

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.580
<i>I quit because I was a disgrace!</i>

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:12.660
<i>Everyone expected great things from me
and watched me like hawks.</i>

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.830
<i>And so, this "average" fourth grader</i>

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.150
<i>got exposed and shamed
over something he never asked for!</i>

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:21.920
<i>I became isolated from my teammates.</i>

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:25.930
<i>Stepping out onto the field became 
nothing but a source of pain.</i>

00:07:27.900 --> 00:07:29.880
<i>If only I wasn't Shigeno Jr...</i>

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.600
<i>If only I wasn't the "second,"
I could've played baseball so freely.</i>

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.240
<i>If only I wasn't the "second"!</i>

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:52.910
Sis!

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.810
What are you going to do about this?!

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:58.640
It broke because you threw it yesterday!

00:07:58.640 --> 00:07:59.820
Pay me back!

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.480
I want the newest model!

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:14.430
I keep telling you not to come into 
the bathroom when I'm in here.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:16.960
I'm... I'm sorry.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:20.560
Oh, you're right.

00:08:20.560 --> 00:08:24.500
See? It's obviously because you 
threw it on the ground yesterday!

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.010
I'm sorry.

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:27.660
Well, it's actually a good thing.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:31.540
This is god's way of telling you
to find a better hobby.

00:08:31.540 --> 00:08:32.360
Say what?

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.630
God conveniently pops up to
tell me that right after you break it?

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:37.930
Quit trying to weasel out of this
and buy me a new one!

00:08:37.930 --> 00:08:39.820
You're so annoying.

00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:41.620
I don't have that kind of money right now.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.430
My glove's almost threadbare,
so I have to replace it...

00:08:46.020 --> 00:08:50.130
That reminds me, you have a glove 
you only used for a year!

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:56.050
Give me that! Then, I can give you 
enough money to repair this thing.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:59.400
Uh, well... I don't have it anymore.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.640
Huh? You don't? Why not?

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.140
I... I threw it away. Ages ago.

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:09.100
I didn't want to see any 
baseball stuff anymore.

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:13.450
Are you serious?! Pop got 
that glove specifically for you—

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:15.400
We're here!

00:09:15.400 --> 00:09:17.070
Good evening.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.040
Wow!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:27.980
What do you think? I caught it myself.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:30.160
We couldn't finish it by ourselves.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:33.600
Grandpa, I think your 
fishing skills are improving.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:36.840
Yep! And I'm gonna keep bringing 
you guys the whoppers!

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:38.820
Okay, let's eat.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:41.920
Go ahead and dig in.
Do you like it?

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:42.340
Yeah, let's eat!

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:43.930
<i>The pitcher winds up...</i>

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:45.350
<i>He hits it!</i>

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:49.930
Oh, I think the Oceans might just make it 
to the Climax Series again this year.

00:09:49.930 --> 00:09:51.260
I don't know about that...

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:54.170
They're 1.5 games behind
the Warriors in fourth.

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:57.990
I like the kid on second base. He recently
stepped up from their second team.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:00.290
Yes! I know what you mean!

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:04.590
Thanks for the food.

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.470
You've finished already?

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:07.400
Yes.

00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.460
He still gets like that when 
people talk about baseball, huh?

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:15.130
Yes.

00:10:15.400 --> 00:10:17.590
A real problem child, that one.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:21.930
Goro also had a pro 
baseball player as a father.

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:28.000
But he never found that to be a burden.

00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:32.340
Well, that man is totally baseball mad.

00:10:32.840 --> 00:10:38.660
I wish Izumi and Daigo could enjoy baseball
free from all the pressure, too.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:39.700
Right.

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:43.910
Well, Goro had Satou Toshiya.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:47.780
Maybe things would be different
if Daigo had a baseball buddy like him.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.040
Tashiro

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.580
Oh, the phone.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:54.040
<i>Bang!</i>

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.300
Hello, Tashiro-kun?

00:10:58.560 --> 00:10:59.340
What?

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.820
Why does everyone only 
care about baseball?

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:12.160
Daigo?

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:13.910
What is it?

00:11:13.910 --> 00:11:17.530
Manager Tashiro of the Dolphins just called.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:18.460
Huh?

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:23.390
Apparently, three players 
have come down with the flu.

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:27.290
So they're short-handed for tomorrow's
match and asked if you could play.

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:28.660
What?!

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:33.660
He said there was no one else he could 
turn to, so I told him it was okay.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:34.780
It <i>is</i> all right, isn't it?

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:41.810
Why?!

00:11:49.110 --> 00:11:50.560
Daigo!

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:55.370
Daigo!

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:00.010
Hey, Daigo, it's 9 o'clock!

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:01.690
How long are you going to sleep?

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:04.330
The match starts at ten!

00:12:04.330 --> 00:12:06.870
We told Manager Tashiro
we'd be there, so hurry up!

00:12:08.090 --> 00:12:10.440
If you don't go, they can't play the match!

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.260
It'll ruin it for everyone!

00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.000
I've had enough of your crap!

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.510
What is wrong with you?

00:12:22.510 --> 00:12:24.820
Why do you have to be so dead set against it?

00:12:24.820 --> 00:12:28.470
It's a practice match, so you just 
have to be a body on the field.

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:32.640
Are you really going to 
buy me a new console?

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:35.600
If you play properly.

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:40.250
Even if you're just making up the numbers,
you have to take it seriously.

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:44.730
Oh, there you are.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:46.410
Tashiro-kun!

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:48.170
Oh, you came!

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:49.910
Thanks, Kaoru-chan!

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:53.370
Sorry for asking you to 
help us out like this, Daigo.

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:54.870
It's no big deal.

00:12:54.870 --> 00:12:57.730
Just so you know, I might drag the team down.

00:12:57.730 --> 00:12:59.290
I suck royally, after all.

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:00.430
Daigo!

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.090
N-No, it's okay.

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:05.260
Daigo, go get changed right away.

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.680
There's a silver van in the parking lot.

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:16.020
I'm sorry that he's still so negative.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:17.790
It's all right.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:23.570
I consider it my failure as a coach that
I couldn't make him stick to baseball.

00:13:24.040 --> 00:13:29.580
I'm pretty sure it's killing him
just to be here today.

00:13:32.130 --> 00:13:33.540
I guess this is it.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:36.690
So they're cruising around in 
a fancy van like this now, huh?

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:45.880
S-Satou?!

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:48.600
Oh, Daigo-kun. So you came.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:50.610
Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:53.470
Wait, if you're wearing 
that uniform, that means...

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:57.290
I went ahead and joined the Dolphins today.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:01.310
For me, a local baseball 
team is enough for now.

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:05.570
Huh? But I was called because 
they didn't have enough people.

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:09.170
Right. Coach said you'll 
be the one playing today.

00:14:09.720 --> 00:14:13.520
I only just joined, so he doesn't 
know if I'm any good or not.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:16.340
He told me to watch from the bench today.

00:14:18.300 --> 00:14:20.500
Hey, Daigo, what's taking so long?!

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:22.090
Get changed already!

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.120
We're about to start!

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:24.840
Okay, okay!

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:28.840
Oh, it's Daigo.

00:14:29.460 --> 00:14:31.240
Hey, long time no see!

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:32.420
Oh, yeah...

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.640
So who's the backup?

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:38.730
I guess you younger guys don't know him.

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.980
That's Shigeno Daigo. He was here for 
a year when we were in fourth grade.

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:45.980
He's the only son of the Shigeno family, 
the ones who gave us the team van.

00:14:46.230 --> 00:14:47.920
Oh, I see.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.860
<i>So that's the deal with the van...</i>

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:50.740
Hey!

00:14:51.240 --> 00:14:55.870
Today, the Dolphins have two descendants 
of former Major League players!

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:59.290
Gorgeous and fantastic, don't you think?

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.230
Stop that! Get off of me!

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:03.630
What's wrong with you, 
bragging about being a "second"?

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:06.340
I wasn't bragging or anything.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.920
Hey, gather round!

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:12.970
Bow!

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.960
Let's have a good game!

00:15:19.060 --> 00:15:20.630
So you put Daigo in right field?

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:21.300
Yeah.

00:15:21.820 --> 00:15:23.480
It's the least stressful position.

00:15:24.010 --> 00:15:27.490
He hasn't played in a long time, 
so it's enough that he's on the field.

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:30.770
<i>What the hell am I doing?</i>

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:34.840
<i>I don't want to see my old teammates.</i>

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:39.040
<i>It's hot, and I can't be bothered.
I just want to go home.</i>

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:46.510
<i>And yet, the feeling of the uniform 
and the smell of the glove...</i>

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:49.380
Play ball!

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:54.640
<i>And the indescribable feeling of anxiety 
and excitement when you hear those words.</i>

00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:58.850
<i>It feels so nostalgic.</i>

00:15:59.140 --> 00:16:00.380
Daigo!

00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:03.600
Good luck! Fight!

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:04.480
<i>Damn, she's close!</i>

00:16:05.010 --> 00:16:06.860
<i>"Fight," my butt.</i>

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.570
<i>Right fielders basically never have to—</i>

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:09.320
It's coming your way!

00:16:11.150 --> 00:16:12.070
Right field!

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:20.080
Out!

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:21.160
He caught it!

00:16:21.160 --> 00:16:22.120
Nice one, right fielder!

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:23.920
Well done, Daigo!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:30.880
<i>For someone who doesn't want to be 
here, he sure is showing some hustle.</i>

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:32.370
Coach...

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.140
Why did Shigeno quit playing baseball?

00:16:36.660 --> 00:16:39.140
I don't really know.

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:43.100
He said he sucked and it wasn't fun for him.

00:16:44.100 --> 00:16:49.360
Huh? But looking at him now, 
he doesn't seem that bad.

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:54.360
It's not like everyone else on 
the team is super great, either.

00:16:54.850 --> 00:16:57.560
So it's not a case of not 
being able to keep up, right?

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.020
Don't throw it! You're too late!

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:02.380
Go for it!

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:04.120
What?

00:17:06.060 --> 00:17:07.710
Their right fielder got there really fast!

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:15.720
Oh, no!

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:19.600
Safe!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.270
All right!

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.600
We were lucky that right fielder's
got a weak arm!

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:29.600
That's the number one reason he quit.

00:17:30.500 --> 00:17:33.500
He's not actually as bad as he thinks he is.

00:17:33.930 --> 00:17:36.240
His defense got quite good
after some practice, too.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:39.870
And he has the baseball IQ to make
smart plays like the backing up just then.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.320
However...

00:17:42.650 --> 00:17:43.970
He's got a weak arm.

00:17:44.740 --> 00:17:50.960
For Daigo, who's always dreamed of
emulating his father as a player,

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:55.970
that gap between dreams and reality
must've felt devastating and unacceptable.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.970
Team

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.970
Guts

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:02.970
Dolphins

00:18:03.250 --> 00:18:04.780
Ball four!

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.380
Okay! Nice eye!

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:09.760
The bases are loaded! 
It's a big chance!

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:11.150
Who's next?

00:18:13.560 --> 00:18:14.690
It's Daigo.

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:18.110
What's the matter?

00:18:18.320 --> 00:18:21.010
Is Shigeno bad at batting as well?

00:18:21.010 --> 00:18:23.400
That doesn't even begin to describe it.

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.190
I can't remember him ever getting a hit.

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:27.870
It's not just your memory.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:31.710
There's no record of him
ever getting a hit in a match.

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:37.710
<i>The pitcher has been 
throwing ball after ball.</i>

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:39.700
<i>I need to take my time and watch.</i>

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.560
Go Daigo!

00:18:41.560 --> 00:18:44.140
Show them the homerun skills 
you got from your dad!

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.380
With your DNA, you can hit it!

00:18:52.950 --> 00:18:55.320
Those were all balls! Watch more closely!

00:18:55.530 --> 00:18:59.280
<i>Dammit. Those guys just 
had to shoot their mouths off!</i>

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:03.490
Strike! Batter out!

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:08.600
Ah, man, we didn't get any runs on the board.

00:19:08.600 --> 00:19:10.500
Our fault for getting our hopes up.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.830
Daigo! There's always next time!

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:14.200
Don't let it get you down!

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:19.100
<i>Must be nice. Mom's so carefree.</i>

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:22.910
<i>For me, baseball is nothing 
but a source of pain.</i>

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:30.650
Stop! Stop!

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.980
All right! One out,
and runners on the corners!

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:36.660
This isn't good.

00:19:37.860 --> 00:19:38.890
Kimura?

00:19:42.730 --> 00:19:46.290
I'm sorry. It looks like 
I twisted my arm just now.

00:19:46.840 --> 00:19:48.200
This is bad.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.720
We're already short today.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:51.330
What do we do?

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:55.220
We have no choice. We can't push him.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:57.300
Satou!

00:19:58.040 --> 00:19:59.600
I'm putting you in!

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:04.130
Are you sure about this, Tashiro?

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:07.330
Satou only joined the team today.
 We don't know anything about him.

00:20:07.330 --> 00:20:09.810
What other choice do we 
have in this situation?

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:12.100
Kishimoto, move to shortstop!

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.980
Satou, you take center field!

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:16.700
All right, leave it to me.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:20.360
To be honest, I was getting 
bored of just watching.

00:20:20.560 --> 00:20:22.340
R-Right...

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:27.830
<i>Is he really going to play now?</i>

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:34.420
<i>Dammit! How can he be that 
calm for his first match?</i>

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.590
<i>Now, they're going to judge 
who the better "second" is...</i>

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:40.890
So how much did he play in the States?

00:20:40.890 --> 00:20:42.120
I don't know.

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:44.840
All I know about him
is that he's Satou's son.

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:48.190
Well, I guess we can just see 
how he does in this match.

00:20:49.040 --> 00:20:49.750
Play!

00:20:50.590 --> 00:20:52.140
Knock it outta the park!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:53.810
We're counting on you, Arizaka!

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:57.770
<i>We've got one out. If nothing else, 
I'll get the runner on third home!</i>

00:21:02.890 --> 00:21:04.140
Center!

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.240
Good enough for a sac fly!

00:21:07.430 --> 00:21:08.640
It's going right to him!

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:10.830
We can see how good Satou Jr.'s arm is!

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:11.370
Kill 'em!

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:26.550
Excuse me?

00:21:26.550 --> 00:21:28.930
All right! Both of you, run!

00:21:28.930 --> 00:21:30.810
Arizaka, run to second!

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:33.640
What's he doing?!

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.840
H-Hey! Go pick it up already!

00:21:35.840 --> 00:21:37.730
Oh, dear. Now, I've gone and done it.

00:21:38.110 --> 00:21:39.480
What are you playing at?!

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:41.770
Throw it back already!
They'll get an inside-the-park homerun!

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:45.210
Give it to me. Your throw won't 
get there before it's too late.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:47.160
You can make it home, Arizaka!

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:09.700
You idiot! What are you aiming it?!

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:10.620
Oh, dear. I've done it again.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:13.200
H-Hey! Are you just messing around?

00:22:13.510 --> 00:22:15.520
First, you miss an easy fly ball,

00:22:15.520 --> 00:22:18.350
then you have a strong arm,
but your control is non-existent!

00:22:18.350 --> 00:22:20.770
Weren't you playing in the 
American little leagues?!

00:22:21.020 --> 00:22:25.030
Huh? This is the first time 
I've ever played baseball.

00:22:25.660 --> 00:22:27.160
What?!

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:02.540
A total newcomer to baseball?!

00:24:03.140 --> 00:24:05.540
Even though he's Satou Toshiya's son?

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:09.730
But, then... how can he make plays like that?

00:24:10.670 --> 00:24:12.060
Satou Hikaru...

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:17.320
Is it possible he got all 
the talent I wanted for myself?

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:25.020
The Two Juniors

00:24:18.620 --> 00:24:21.140
Next time: The Two Juniors

00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:23.610
Run to the stage of your dreams!
